Title: The Last Diner
Author: Example

FADE IN:

EXT. DESERT HIGHWAY - DUSK

A lone neon sign flickers over an empty two-lane road. A dusty pickup rolls to a stop.

MARA OKAFOR (30s), a lanky mechanic with a shaved head and oil-stained denim overalls, climbs out and stretches.

INT. LAST CHANCE DINER - NIGHT

Chrome stools, cracked red vinyl. Behind the counter, EDDIE (60s), a heavyset cook with a white beard and a grease-spotted apron, wipes a mug.

MARA
(tired)
Coffee. Black. Whatever's left in the pot.

EDDIE
Pot's been dead since noon. I'll make fresh.

Mara drops onto a stool and pulls a crumpled map from her pocket.

MARA
How far to Barstow?

EDDIE (O.S.)
Too far for tonight.

EXT. DINER PARKING LOT - NIGHT

[[SCENE LOOK MARA: soaked from the rain, hair dripping]]

Rain hammers the lot. Mara, now wearing a borrowed yellow raincoat, checks the pickup's engine with a flashlight.

YOUNG MARA
Dad, is it fixed yet?

CUT TO:

INT. LAST CHANCE DINER - LATER

[[LOOK EDDIE: reset]]

Eddie slides a plate of eggs across the counter. Mara eats like she hasn't in days.

EDDIE
Stay. Storm'll pass by morning.

MARA
It always does.

FADE OUT.
